title: 'xcm-executor: price the end-of-message refund and stop buying back a refund holding cannot take'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The surplus refund the executor runs at the end of every message was never charged. It is
    now charged the weigher's weight of a `RefundSurplus`, kept out of the refund and counted in
    the weight used, but only when the trader refunds something. The charge is taken per weight
    dimension: a dimension whose surplus does not cover it is not refunded, and a surplus that
    covers it in no dimension is left as it was.

    The `buy_execution`, `pay_fees` and `refund_surplus` benchmarks now mint the asset of
    `pallet_xcm_benchmarks::generic::Config::worst_case_for_trader` into holding when
    `worst_case_holding` does not have it. A runtime whose trader swaps, such as one with
    `SwapFirstAssetTrader`, should return an asset the trader swaps from `worst_case_for_trader`,
    so the weights of `BuyExecution`, `PayFees` and `RefundSurplus` include the swap. Asset Hub
    Westend now does.

    A refund is no longer bought back from the trader when holding is at capacity. `RefundSurplus`
    now fails with `HoldingWouldOverflow` before asking the trader when holding is at capacity for
    the refund, if execution was paid for, or the leftover `fees`, even when their assets are in
    holding, and leaves both to the end of the message. There, holding takes the refund and any leftover `fees` regardless of
    its capacity and is trapped for the claimer as usual. Before, the trader bought the refund back,
    or dropped it when the buy-back failed, as it always did for `TakeFirstAssetTrader`, and the
    leftover `fees` were dropped with the executor; both are now claimable.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    A message that still has unrefunded surplus weight when it ends is charged the weight of one
    `RefundSurplus` for the refund the executor makes on its behalf, so the refund is that much
    smaller, and no refund is made when the surplus does not cover it. This applies after an
    explicit `RefundSurplus` too when surplus accrues later, for example from an error handler
    that never ran.
crates:
- name: staging-xcm-executor
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-xcm-benchmarks
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
